<title>FINLAND: Kesko buys units from its Tuko.</title>
<headline>Kesko buys units from its Tuko.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish wholesaler Kesko Oy said in a statement on Friday it had bought units from Tuko for 635 million markka to strengthen Tuko's financial position.</p>
<p>&quot;Kesko has bought Anttila Oy's share capital from Tuko for 420 million markka and Tuko Oy's Hameenkyla central warehouse building and operations for 215 million markka in total,&quot; Kesko said.</p>
<p>The deals will not affect Anttila's organisation or operations, it said, adding that the EU had been notified of the deals.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358 - 0 - 680 50 245</p>
